      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Toxicity is genus-level: the NC State page is for Dracaena reflexa var. angustifolia (red-marginated dracaena), a related name, not D. marginata itself; Clemson's page does not mention toxicity. Hence from_knowledge_verify. Size: dragon tree up to 10 ft, upright types usually under 2 ft wide (Clemson). The Missouri Botanical Garden page failed (certificate error). Interval: NC State (genus page) 'allow plants to dry between waterings but not severely', drought tolerant; Missouri Botanical Garden 'keep soils uniformly moist during growing season, reduce fall to late winter', leaves brown if too wet or too dry. The two split between dry-between and uniformly moist, so 12 stays unconfirmed (review). Clemson let_top_dry (earlier read) sides with NC State. Pot and season: 13 cm pot, bright indirect light, room temperature, growing season. Dry and wet tolerance days: no source gives days, left as before."
      },
